				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T16:14:51.407Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://cosocial.ca/@boris\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>boris</span></a></span> ah just for the record I don’t think this *changes* their stance on whether or not they will pursue hosting—previously Netlify was the official hosting partner.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110968185653743698",
			"parentId": "110968130201144246",
			"url": "https://cosocial.ca/@boris/110968185570454166",
			"author": {
				"name": "Boris Mann",
				"url": "https://cosocial.ca/@boris",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/110/118/955/928/962/297/original/35ae22c59e006661.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-28T16:28:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> for sure, it just means that there’s a blank space that isn’t hosting where we need to imagine paid services. </p><p>Having already switched official partners, we know that hosting isn’t tightly coupled in the open source framework.</p>",
