			"date": "2023-08-29T13:10:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.xyz/@remotesynth\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>remotesynth</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> If I’m correct, Vercel owns and maintains Next, but Svelte is “owned” 100% by <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://toot.cafe/@rich_harris\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>rich_harris</span></a></span>.</p><p>Vue/Nuxt are not “belonging” to any other corpo.</p>",
